Among the following types of reasoning, which one is deductive reasoning?
A: From the fact that gold, silver, copper, and iron conduct electricity, it is inferred that all metals conduct electricity;
B: It is inferred that the general formula for the sequence $\dfrac{1}{1\times 2},\dfrac{1}{2\times 3},\dfrac{1}{3\times 4},\ldots$ is $a_n=\dfrac{1}{n(n+1)}(n\in N_+)$;
C: Given that the area $S$ of a circle with radius $r$ is $S=\pi r^2$, it is inferred that the area $S$ of a unit circle is $\pi$;
D: From the equation of a circle in the Cartesian coordinate system being $(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2$, it is inferred that the equation of a sphere in the three-dimensional Cartesian coordinate system is $(x-a)^2+(y-b)^2+(z-c)^2=r^2$.

